# Build-context exclusions for the Quanta CMS base image (quanta/Dockerfile).
# Everything here is either rebuilt during the image build (vendor, the Rust
# target dir) or irrelevant at runtime — keeping it out speeds up the context
# upload and prevents stale artifacts leaking into the image.
#
# The image's `COPY . /var/www/quanta/` puts whatever survives this file under
# the document root, so an exclusion here is also an exclusion from the web
# root: anything that is not application code has no business being there.

.git
.githooks
.github
.idea
.idea*
*.swp
**/.DS_Store

# Composer output — regenerated by `composer install` inside the image.
vendor
vendor/*
composer.lock

# Runtime/site data — mounted as volumes, never baked in.
sites
sites/*
_sites
_sites/*
static/tmp
static/tmp/*

# qdb: only Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock and src/ are needed to compile the
# extension. The Rust target dir (huge) and the test/demo assets are not.
qdb/target
qdb/demo
qdb/tests/bench
qdb/.gitignore

# Development, CI and build material. None of it is read at runtime, and all of
# it would otherwise sit inside the document root. quanta-nginx.conf belongs to
# a native (non-container) install — the image's vhost is docker/nginx/ — and
# .conf is not among the extensions deny-dev-files.conf blocks.
docs
tests
.phpcs.xml
package.json
contacts.csv
quanta-nginx.conf
Dockerfile
.dockerignore

# A Stripe test key, unreferenced by any code in this repo. Whatever it is for,
# a credentials file under the document root is not it — a site that needs one
# gets it from its .env (see docker-entrypoint.sh).
secrets.php
